            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          },
          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582783,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Early Interest in Photography and Film</strong><br>\nStanley Kubrick was born in New York City on July 26, 1928. He developed an interest in photography in high school, which led to a job as a photographer for Look magazine. His early photography work displayed the keen eye for composition and lighting that would become hallmarks of his films.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Transition to Filmmaking</strong><br>\nKubrick's transition from photographer to filmmaker began with short documentaries in the late 1940s. By 1953, he had directed his first feature film, \"Fear and Desire.\" He worked independently, which allowed him complete artistic control but also required him to be involved in all aspects of filmmaking.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Acclaim and Unique Style</strong><br>\nKubrick gained acclaim with \"Paths of Glory\" (1957) and the commercial success \"Spartacus\" (1960). His unique style became evident through his use of innovative camera techniques, deep focus, and long tracking shots, as well as his preference for natural light.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "53bc5361-5ce5-43a9-a00f-57bbceee9cd0"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          }
        ],
        "slideBackgroundSelector": {}
      },
      {
        "elements": [
          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
