          {
            "x": 2.178649237472767,
            "y": 12.910611231371064,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Collaborations with Actors and Writers</strong><br>\nKubrick's selective filmography reflects his meticulous nature and demand for perfection, leading to intense collaborations with actors and writers. He often worked with renowned actors like Jack Nicholson and writers like Arthur C. Clarke, ensuring that every element aligned with his vision.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Influence on Film and Culture</strong><br>\nKubrick's work has profoundly influenced the art of filmmaking, with his meticulous approach to detail and his thematic ambitions. His films often provoke discussion and have become cultural landmarks within the history of cinema.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Legacy and Posthumous Recognition</strong><br>\nKubrick passed away on March 7, 1999, leaving behind films that continue to be celebrated for their innovation, depth, and vision. His legacy persists in the directors he influenced and in the timeless quality of his cinematic achievements.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
